[Event "Basic tactics: the fork, lesson"]
[Result "1-0"]
[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/oLCBkefa/xAXNBsdf"]
[Role "teaching"]
[Variant "Standard"]
[FEN "8/5q1p/8/5NK1/6P1/3k4/8/8 b - - 11 52"]
[SetUp "1"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/8/5q1p/8/5NK1/6P1/3k4/8/8_b_-_-_11_52"]

{ Welcome to tactics school. A tactic is a trick that wins material, and today you learn six of them. You are White. First the fork: one move, two targets, and he can only save one. }
52... Ke4 { His king steps up to help his queen, and that is a mistake: a check with his queen would have kept him safe. Now his king and his queen are a single knight jump from the same square. Land there and you hit both at once. [%csl Re4,Rf7][%cal Yf5d6] } 53. Nd6+ { Check, and every legal move he has left is a king move. While he is saving his king, his queen gets no chance to run. [%cal Gd6e4,Gd6f7] } (53. Nh6 { Your knight attacks his queen, but there is no check, so she simply strolls away and you have won nothing at all. } 53... Qe7+ 54. Kh5 { She left with a check of her own, and now his queen hunts your king along the edge and forces mate. [%csl Rh5] }) (53. Ne7 { Your knight lands right beside his queen with nothing guarding it, so she eats it for free. } 53... Qxe7+ 54. Kh6 { Your knight is gone, one lonely pawn is all you have left, and his queen mates your king in three. [%csl Rh6] }) 53... Kd5 { His king runs, and his queen is still sitting on exactly the square your knight attacks. Go and take her. [%cal Yd6f7] } 54. Nxf7 { His queen is yours and nothing can take your knight back. One knight, two targets, and he could save only one: that is a fork. } (54. Nf5 { Your knight scuttles home and lets his queen off the hook, and both targets vanish in a single move. } 54... Ke5 55. Nh4 Qf4+ { His queen checks you and starts hunting your king. A knight and a pawn cannot hold her off, and he has a forced mate. [%cal Rf4g5] }) 1-0


