{ You are White, and the material is close. His queen is deep in your camp, your king has lost its pawn cover, and it looks like you are the one in trouble. [%csl Rh3] }
18... Qxe6 { His queen takes your knight, and he is two pawns up. Taking was the mistake: his knight should have come out instead. Find the move that turns the game around. } 19. Bg4 { Your bishop pins his queen to his king: she is standing on the line between them and cannot step off it. [%cal Gg4e6,Ge6c8] } (19. Bd2 { A quiet developing move, and his knight comes out to cover the square your bishop needed. } 19... Nf6 20. Qe1 { He is two pawns up, his pieces are coming out, and the chance you had has quietly gone. [%csl Rc8] }) (19. Rf4 { Your rook steps up the column, but it attacks nothing and it traps nothing at all. } 19... Kb8 20. Bd2 { You have gained nothing, he is still two pawns up, and his king has walked out of the pin. [%csl Rb8] }) (19. Qxd5 { You grab the pawn in the middle, and his rook takes your queen. [%cal Rd8d5] } 19... Rxd5 { A queen for a pawn. The game is lost. [%csl Rd5] }) (19. Rf2 { A quiet rook move, and his knight comes out to guard everything. } 19... Nf6 20. Rf4 Be4 { His pieces are out, his bishop aims at the corner beside your king, and he is two pawns up. He is winning. [%cal Re4h1] }) (19. Rf3 { Your rook steps up, and his queen checks you first. } 19... Qg4+ 20. Kf1 Be4 { His bishop attacks your rook, his queen is safe, and he is two pawns up. He is winning. [%cal Re4f3] }) 19... Qxg4+ { His queen is stuck on that line, so she takes your bishop, and it arrives with a check you have to answer. } 20. Qxg4+ { Your queen takes his, with check. A queen for a bishop: she was pinned to her king and could not leave that line. That is the pin, and from two pawns behind you have a winning game. } (20. Kh2 { You step out of the check and let his queen live, which throws away everything the pin had won. } 20... Qh4+ 21. Kg2 { His queen and bishop are hunting your king now and he has a forced mate. You gave a bishop and got nothing back. [%csl Rg2] }) (20. Kf2 { You step out of the check and leave his queen alive. Now his rook joins the hunt. } 20... Rf8+ 21. Ke1 Rxf1+ { His rook takes yours with check, and your queen goes next. Mate is close. [%csl Re1] }) (20. Kh1 { Into the corner, with his queen still on the board. His bishop checks straight away. } 20... Be4+ 21. Rf3 Rd6 { His rook swings across, and mate on the edge cannot be stopped. [%cal Rd6h6] }) 1-0


